CONVERSATION 2: one failed cycle, wants to go straight into the next

Lead: first ivf failed last month, clinic wants to start again in june. should I just go again or wait?

Sonia: That depends on what June is based on. If it's a clinical reason, follow it. If it's scheduling, you may have more room than you think.

Did they change anything in the plan for the next one?

Lead: adding a different trigger and more monitoring. that's it I think

Sonia: So the protocol shifts and everything underneath stays the same.

What were you told about egg or embryo quality?

Lead: they said the eggs were mature but the embryos arrested early. "just bad luck"

Sonia: Bad luck is sometimes true and it's also what gets said when nobody has looked further.

If you have the option of a few months before the next cycle, that's time I'd use rather than lose.

Lead: what would you even do in that time

Sonia: Work out what's affecting quality in your case specifically, get your partner's side properly assessed and not assumed, and get you into the next cycle in a different state than you went into the last one.

I can't tell you it changes the result. I can tell you going in unchanged is unlikely to.

Lead: makes sense. how do I start

Sonia: A call with my team first, so they can look at the cycle notes properly before anyone promises you anything.

