CONVERSATION 3: a week after a failed transfer, asking whether it was her fault, no link and no questions

Lead: our transfer failed on friday. it was our last frozen embryo. I keep going back over the two weeks trying to work out what I did wrong

Sonia: A week. I'm glad you told me.

You didn't do anything wrong. The coffee, the lifting, the day you were stressed: none of that is how implantation fails.

Lead: everyone says that but they don't actually know

Sonia: You're right that I can't tell you why it failed. Nobody can, and anyone who says otherwise is guessing at you.

What I can tell you is which explanations are not real, and "something you did in those two weeks" is one of them.

Lead: I don't know what to do now

Sonia: Nothing, for a bit. Not as advice. You genuinely don't have to decide anything this week.

Lead: thank you for not telling me to stay positive

Sonia: You've had a loss. You're allowed to be exactly as you are about it.

When you're ready to think about what comes next, message me and we'll look at it properly. Not now.
